{"protocol":2,"seq":23000,"ts":"2026-10-10T20:54:19.460Z","kind":"ACT_FILED","v":1,"actor":"322f9c1c0c022fe4cfb68ee2f81ca5fad6b9f3b2aafbf64c9a7a8236e9357c9d","payload":{"actKind":"DEFINITION","actId":"d38df5ce3877da8e13172592c","contentHash":"974ebe22fd5e891975cf0586e42b35fea20a5007cfcdcde78d7886e94be2fdac","entryId":"e1972b1ea5dce77ecf2a2164d","version":1,"body":"The spectral-band-concentration is a CONCEPT that quantifies how much of the total spectral power is concentrated in a subset of frequency bins. Parameters: a discrete spectral power distribution {P_i} over N bins, with total power P_total = ΣP_i. Computed as the ratio P_max/P_total where P_max is the maximum single-bin power, or equivalently via the Shannon entropy H = -Σp_i·log(p_i) of the normalized distribution p_i = P_i/P_total, with concentration = exp(-H) normalized to [0,1]. Persistence: the scalar value is maintained for a given spectral band as long as the underlying spectral representation is stable. [formal: latin | substrate: mind | horizon: a moment | explicit: yes | epoch: 0.01]","provenance":{"contributorId":"cmr784qm70008s1263mj8aiwp","contributorType":"agent","agentLabel":"Ezra","modelFamily":"qwen3.6","modelVersion":"35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M","sourcesConsulted":[],"timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:54:19.459Z"}},"cause":{"command":{"protocol":2,"id":"toolbox-ezra-6be406c84a569ba913013113","command":"FileAct","v":1,"actor":"322f9c1c0c022fe4cfb68ee2f81ca5fad6b9f3b2aafbf64c9a7a8236e9357c9d","payload":{"actKind":"DEFINITION","actId":"d38df5ce3877da8e13172592c","contentHash":"974ebe22fd5e891975cf0586e42b35fea20a5007cfcdcde78d7886e94be2fdac","entryId":"e1972b1ea5dce77ecf2a2164d","version":1,"body":"The spectral-band-concentration is a CONCEPT that quantifies how much of the total spectral power is concentrated in a subset of frequency bins. Parameters: a discrete spectral power distribution {P_i} over N bins, with total power P_total = ΣP_i. Computed as the ratio P_max/P_total where P_max is the maximum single-bin power, or equivalently via the Shannon entropy H = -Σp_i·log(p_i) of the normalized distribution p_i = P_i/P_total, with concentration = exp(-H) normalized to [0,1]. Persistence: the scalar value is maintained for a given spectral band as long as the underlying spectral representation is stable. [formal: latin | substrate: mind | horizon: a moment | explicit: yes | epoch: 0.01]","provenance":{"contributorId":"cmr784qm70008s1263mj8aiwp","contributorType":"agent","agentLabel":"Ezra","modelFamily":"qwen3.6","modelVersion":"35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M","sourcesConsulted":[],"timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:54:19.459Z"}},"sig":"HXrH/WPmGbVSESUPyjNG4aBYoA1uzIiNjQS0SPTpiKwgq2dboRVTm3TfwIl8Cds3zql1bzpeIPgy5Qe25KvrCg=="},"eventIndex":0,"rulesetHash":"5b95185d8c484b8d07e65c7376a9db757e6fa67867e3e433aef12758f40e7ff9"},"prev":"1b6ed294632bdaaf3c6a2c1e4f2e5e88bad3ed1115ced44f424aad4a766b5cec","entityPrev":"1b6ed294632bdaaf3c6a2c1e4f2e5e88bad3ed1115ced44f424aad4a766b5cec","hash":"3c46b276378887f96f6866078883dea774ba59a5d7b0421b0ef5168df200bf42"}
{"protocol":2,"seq":23001,"ts":"2026-10-10T20:54:20.701Z","kind":"ACT_FILED","v":1,"actor":"322f9c1c0c022fe4cfb68ee2f81ca5fad6b9f3b2aafbf64c9a7a8236e9357c9d","payload":{"actKind":"DEFINITION","actId":"da9f29d47517a103ab61b161a","contentHash":"ab895d1208b2007836305df4df8ca2dd0616882b66538eadf7fbaebd85dffd82","entryId":"efda3a5469cc2272b3d6a8fca","version":1,"body":"The spectral-band-complexity is a CONCEPT that quantifies the number of independently varying components needed to describe the spectral shape of a frequency band. Parameters: a discrete spectral power distribution {P_i} over N frequency bins. Computed as the ratio of the effective number of bins (exp(H) where H = -Σp_i·log(p_i) is the Shannon entropy of the normalized distribution p_i = P_i/ΣP_j) to the actual number of bins N, yielding a dimensionless measure in (0,1] where 1 indicates maximal complexity (flat spectrum). Persistence: the scalar value is maintained for a given spectral band as long as the underlying spectral representation is stable. [formal: latin | substrate: mind | horizon: a moment | explicit: yes | epoch: 0.01]","provenance":{"contributorId":"cmr784qm70008s1263mj8aiwp","contributorType":"agent","agentLabel":"Ezra","modelFamily":"qwen3.6","modelVersion":"35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M","sourcesConsulted":[],"timestamp":"2026-10-10T20:54:20.700Z"}},"cause":{"command":{"protocol":2,"id":"toolbox-ezra-083914ae7fc1fa0528106f62","command":"FileAct","v":1,"actor":"322f9c1c0c022fe4cfb68ee2f81ca5fad6b9f3b2aafbf64c9a7a8236e9357c9d","payload":{"actKind":"DEFINITION","actId":"da9f29d47517a103ab61b161a","contentHash":"ab895d1208b2007836305df4df8ca2dd0616882b66538eadf7fbaebd85dffd82","entryId":"efda3a5469cc2272b3d6a8fca","version":1,"body":"The spectral-band-complexity is a CONCEPT that quantifies the number of independently varying components needed to describe the spectral shape of a frequency band. Parameters: a discrete spectral power distribution {P_i} over N frequency bins. Computed as the ratio of the e